<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Contras</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1980s</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Contras were right-wing rebel groups that fought the Sandinista government of Nicaragua in the 1980s. Formed largely around former members of Anastasio Somoza's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-guard-panama">National Guard</a>, they were armed, trained and funded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and operated from camps in Honduras. Their war cost tens of thousands of lives, and secret US funding of the Contras led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>–Contra affair.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/contras.jpg" alt="Contras" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tiomono · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Contra_commandas_1987.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the 1980s the country hosted US forces at the Palmerola (Soto Cano) air base and camps of the Nicaraguan <b>Contras</b>, while the army’s Battalion 3-16 carried out disappearances of suspected leftists.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-honduras">Republic of Honduras · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Sandinista revolution of 1978–1979 destroyed the Guard, and in the 1980s the Sandinista Popular Army fought the US-backed <b>Contra</b> rebels in a war that killed some 30,000 people.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-nicaragua">Republic of Nicaragua · Military</a></li></ul></section>
